ip between our leadership  the congressional black caucus and the  judiciary committee  you have heard and you will hear  eight minutes 46 seconds  i can't breathe a knee  on my neck whether we say  george floyd brianna taylor  or from my district casey goodson andre  hill  or tamir rice that is what i want you to  remember  why we fought so hard  to get this bill right and why we are so  proud to stand here tonight we cannot  bring back  their loss or the pain their families  and friends  have faced but we can fight for  transparency  for accountability for justice  and let me just say as i stood with some  of my colleagues  with george floyd's family tonight  we do this in remembrance  in honor of him and all those who have  lost their lives  senselessly at the hands of law  enforcement  but i want you to remember no matter  what anyone says  this deal is about justice  transparency accountability  and lastly in the words of his  seven-year-old daughter  when she said my daddy  has changed the world tonight i say  as chair of the congressional black  caucus  we stand with our colleagues as we  change the world and that is  our power our message thank you  and now we will hear from the chairwoman  of the  subcommittee on judiciary crime and  terrorism  representative sheila jackson lee  thank you very much congresswoman bass  and thank you  for your leadership uh thank you to our  leaders and as well the congressional  black caucus we worked as a team  and the judiciary committee worked as a  team  let me say that this was so important to  the floyd family  that they wanted to be present  to be able to see the fruition  if you will of the sacrifice  of their brother for he was sacrificed  in a calculated  killing murder on the streets of america  a murder that evidenced itself around  the world  with a grin a smirk on the actor  the police officer that was causing his  death  and causing the words i can't breathe  and so i want to say to his late parents  who  his 